{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794907674,"nonce":"oyHsF2V0cNw6iDrbGMrLMYe39Zo=","title":"Found while validating 68a2308 with hxn-window and the released hxn GPU drivers.","message":"A threaded Emscripten program linking a debug hxn-window package and a release hxn-gpu-webgpu package fails in wasm-ld with duplicate rust_eh_personality and __rustc allocator/exception-handler definitions. The libraries were built with the same rustc (nightly-2026-08-25). Their copies of std have different object identities because the profiles differ, so an object pulled for its Rust-mangled definitions also brings already-defined runtime entry points.\n\nRebuilding the window package with hxn package cpp --wasm --threads --release makes it link with both released browser GPU drivers. WebGPU and WebGL2 presentation then pass in Chrome.\n\nAsh's wasm archive pull handles overlapping definitions explicitly in ash_wasm_link/src/archive.rs: a definition already in the link demotes a later definition to a reference and records it as shadowed. The Emscripten path has no equivalent handling. A general fix should preserve collision checks for a library's public ABI; suppressing all duplicate-definition diagnostics would also hide two libraries exporting the same public entry point.\n\nUntil this is addressed, build threaded wasm packages with the same release profile as the released libraries they are linked with. A regression should link two libraries built with differing profiles and exercise their error and allocation paths.","files":null}]}